      "content": "i get the clash of values thing, but that's kinda vague for a news story. i need to get to the heart of why this is so divisive. if you had to look at the actual impact, isn't it true that the main \"pro\" argument is basically just about liberating families from failing systems? and on the other hand, isn't the opposition mostly just trying to protect the status quo and keep all the money for themselves? like, which side is actually making the more logical case for the kids?",
